/E (The terrorist attacks of 9/11 ushered in an era of remote warfare characterized by the use of large, armed, and networked drones to enhance force protection while removing combatants and reducing collateral damage. Since then, countries have increasingly miniaturized drones. This has led to the emergence of smaller, commercially-available, and easily weaponized drones, such as the Chinese DJI. )
